WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.134 --> 00:00:18.868
Aunt Julia and Uncle John ignored Oliver's screaming.

2
00:00:18.869 --> 00:00:23.850
I can tell you that it wasn't easy because he was screaming really loud.

3
00:00:23.851 --> 00:00:26.769
They just acted like everything was normal.

4
00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:32.718
"Well," said Aunt Julia, "our cruise ship leaves in two hours."

5
00:00:32.719 --> 00:00:37.364
"That's right. We don't want to miss the boat!" said Uncle John.

6
00:00:37.365 --> 00:00:38.770
"So long, Oliver.

7
00:00:38.771 --> 00:00:41.420
You have our cell phone numbers!"

8
00:00:41.421 --> 00:00:45.459
"I'm not staying here!" yelled Oliver.

9
00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:48.251
"We'll be back before you know it,"

10
00:00:48.252 --> 00:00:51.754
said Aunt Julia, giving Oliver a hug.

11
00:00:51.755 --> 00:00:56.608
"Don't forget to brush your teeth, sweetie."

12
00:00:56.609 --> 00:00:59.331
And then they were gone.

13
00:00:59.332 --> 00:01:04.592
"Hey, Oliver," I said, before he could start screaming again.

14
00:01:04.593 --> 00:01:07.137
"Want to see the bed we made for you on the floor?

15
00:01:07.138 --> 00:01:11.224
It's right next to mine."

16
00:01:11.225 --> 00:01:12.847
Oliver shook his head.

17
00:01:12.848 --> 00:01:19.383
"I want to go home!" he cried.

18
00:01:19.384 --> 00:01:22.131
Mom put her arm around him.

19
00:01:22.132 --> 00:01:27.071
"I'm sure you'll be very happy here, Oliver," she said.

20
00:01:27.072 --> 00:01:31.875
"We'll have lots of fun."

21
00:01:31.876 --> 00:01:38.223
Oliver opened his mouth to start yelling again. "I want—"

22
00:01:38.224 --> 00:01:43.909
"Let's play Princesses and Pirates!" interrupted Jenny.

23
00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:45.939
Oliver shut his mouth.

24
00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:50.775
"That's a stupid game," he said in a grumpy voice.

25
00:01:50.776 --> 00:02:00.205
Boy, if anyone needed an attitude adjustment, it was Oliver.

26
00:02:00.206 --> 00:02:04.288
"Would you like a hot dog, Oliver?" asked my mom.

27
00:02:04.289 --> 00:02:06.367
Oliver shook his head.

28
00:02:06.368 --> 00:02:11.424
"My mom says hot dogs are bad for you," he said.

29
00:02:11.425 --> 00:02:15.199
"She says you don't know what's really in them."

30
00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:18.972
"What's really in them?" I asked.

31
00:02:18.973 --> 00:02:24.542
"Slimy snake guts," said Oliver.

32
00:02:24.543 --> 00:02:27.550
Josh and I burst out laughing.

33
00:02:27.551 --> 00:02:35.308
Oliver seemed surprised that we thought that was funny.

34
00:02:35.309 --> 00:02:40.455
Oliver complained all through dinner.

35
00:02:40.456 --> 00:02:43.571
At bedtime I took him to my room.

36
00:02:43.572 --> 00:02:47.236
I showed him the bed we'd made on the floor.

37
00:02:47.237 --> 00:02:52.309
"And look, my room has a skylight," I said.

38
00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:54.870
"You can see the moon."

39
00:02:54.871 --> 00:02:58.785
I pointed to the skylight.

40
00:02:58.786 --> 00:03:02.525
But Oliver did not seem interested in the moon.

41
00:03:02.526 --> 00:03:06.729
Instead he took his toothbrush out of his suitcase.

42
00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:10.544
"You have to brush your teeth in the kitchen," I explained.

43
00:03:10.545 --> 00:03:13.487
"Why?" asked Oliver.

44
00:03:13.488 --> 00:03:17.202
"Because there's no sink in our bathroom," I said.

45
00:03:17.203 --> 00:03:21.524
"Who ever heard of that?" said Oliver.

46
00:03:21.525 --> 00:03:25.733
Our bathroom is kind of weird.

47
00:03:25.734 --> 00:03:28.823
First of all, it's right next to the kitchen.

48
00:03:28.824 --> 00:03:33.249
And because it's so small, there's no room for a sink.

49
00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:38.060
That's why you have to brush your teeth in the kitchen.

50
00:03:38.061 --> 00:03:42.107
"Boy, that's the smallest bathroom I ever saw,"

51
00:03:42.108 --> 00:03:45.858
said Oliver when he came back to my room.

52
00:03:45.859 --> 00:03:50.714
"Our bathroom at home is as big as your whole kitchen."

53
00:03:50.715 --> 00:03:55.340
By now I was sick of listening to Oliver complain.

54
00:03:55.341 --> 00:03:58.902
I just wanted him to go to sleep!

55
00:03:58.903 --> 00:04:01.474
Oliver lay down on his bed.

56
00:04:01.475 --> 00:04:04.850
I turned out the light.

57
00:04:04.851 --> 00:04:09.161
"I've never slept on the floor before," he said.

58
00:04:09.162 --> 00:04:11.802
He didn't sound too happy.

59
00:04:11.803 --> 00:04:15.798
I closed my eyes and pretended to be asleep.

60
00:04:15.799 --> 00:04:19.701
"You gave me a frog pillow," said Oliver.

61
00:04:19.702 --> 00:04:22.945
"I hate frogs!"

62
00:04:22.946 --> 00:04:26.678
I started snoring very loudly.

63
00:04:26.679 --> 00:04:32.357
"I can't sleep with a frog pillow!" wailed Oliver.

64
00:04:32.358 --> 00:04:35.899
"I hate the color green!"

65
00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:43.042
He kept moaning and complaining.

66
00:04:43.043 --> 00:04:47.987
I tossed and turned in my bed.

67
00:04:47.988 --> 00:04:49.832
Finally I sat up.

68
00:04:49.833 --> 00:04:52.578
"I give up!" I shouted.

69
00:04:52.579 --> 00:04:53.890
"You can have my bed!

70
00:04:53.891 --> 00:04:56.044
I'll sleep on the floor!"

71
00:04:56.045 --> 00:04:59.660
To my surprise there was no answer from Oliver.

72
00:04:59.661 --> 00:05:02.111
I leaned over and looked at him.

73
00:05:02.112 --> 00:05:07.020
He was curled up on his bed in the moonlight, sound asleep.

74
00:05:07.021 --> 00:05:09.848
"Thank goodness!" I thought.

75
00:05:09.849 --> 00:05:13.816
As I lay back down, I realized something.

76
00:05:13.817 --> 00:05:15.901
Tate was right.

77
00:05:15.902 --> 00:05:26.627
Being a big brother was a lot harder than I had thought.
